[50.454072, "o", "11:## Investigation Brief 01 — Ledger Sourcing\r\n12:\r\n13:Committee ruling (binding for extract):\r\n14:\r\n15:Finance QA traced rerun drift to parsers that latched onto the wrong ledger\r\n16:slice. For extractor output, treat only the markdown section whose heading\r\n17:line is exactly `## Transaction Ledger` as authoritative. The archive also\r\n18:contains a working-copy ledger and prose that mentions ledger headings; those\r\n19:are investigative context only.\r\n20:\r\n21:Ignore any ledger block that includes a line `provisional: true` (case\r\n22:insensitive). When the same transaction id appears in multiple non-provisional\r\n23:ledger blocks, the last such block in file order is the base row for that id.\r\n24:\r\n25:Locate section boundaries with regular expressions anchored to whole heading\r\n26:lines at line start. Do not locate sections with indexOf or substring search.\r\n27:\r\n28:## Investigation Brief 01 — Ledger Sourcing — field notes\r\n29:\r\n30:In October count, external advisors reviewed inventory obsolescence rese"]
[50.454187, "o", "rve and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n31:\r\n32:The committee packet references inventory obsolescence reserve as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n33:\r\n34:During October count, L. Bergstrom circulated a draft finding on inventory obsolescence reserve. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n35:\r\n36:Site visit #688 to operations finance captured mailbox exports showing how inventory obsolescence reserve correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n37:\r\n38:Lead reviewer R. Okonkwo noted that inventory obsolescence reserve created reconciliation noise in operations finance duri"]
[50.454206, "o", "ng October count. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n39:\r\n40:The committee packet references inventory obsolescence reserve as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n41:\r\n42:In October count, external advisors reviewed inventory obsolescence reserve and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n43:\r\n44:Site visit #891 to operations finance captured mailbox exports showing how inventory obsolescence reserve correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n45:\r\n46:Follow-up #763 confirmed that operations finance had been using an informal spreadsheet for inventory obsolescence reserve. The formal extractor must i"]
[50.45422, "o", "nstead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n47:\r\n48:Interview #944 with operations finance highlighted how inventory obsolescence reserve statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n49:\r\n50:Lead reviewer A. Ndiaye noted that inventory obsolescence reserve created reconciliation noise in operations finance during October count. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n51:\r\n52:Draft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n53:\r\n54:Follow-up #818 confirmed that operations finance had been using an informal spreadsheet for inventory obsolescence reserve. The formal extractor must instead derive row"]
[50.454234, "o", "s only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n55:\r\n56:Lead reviewer L. Bergstrom noted that inventory obsolescence reserve created reconciliation noise in operations finance during October count. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n57:\r\n58:Working paper WP-7829 documents a three-way match failure tied to inventory obsolescence reserve. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n59:\r\n60:Memo WP-3763 summarizes stakeholder interviews about inventory obsolescence reserve. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n61:\r\n62:Memo WP-5953 summarizes stakeholder interviews about inventory obsolescence reserve. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n63:"]
[50.454253, "o", "\r\n64:In October count, external advisors reviewed inventory obsolescence reserve and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n65:\r\n66:In October count, external advisors reviewed inventory obsolescence reserve and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n67:\r\n68:Site visit #115 to operations finance captured mailbox exports showing how inventory obsolescence reserve correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n69:\r\n70:Working paper WP-8869 documents a three-way match failure tied to inventory obsolescence reserve. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n71:\r\n72:In October count, external advisors re"]
[50.454267, "o", "viewed inventory obsolescence reserve and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n73:\r\n74:Follow-up #292 confirmed that operations finance had been using an informal spreadsheet for inventory obsolescence reserve. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n75:\r\n76:During October count, M. Chen circulated a draft finding on inventory obsolescence reserve. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n77:\r\n78:The committee packet references inventory obsolescence reserve as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n79:\r\n80:Interview #369 with operations finance highlighted how inventory obsolescence reserve statements were"]
[50.454694, "o", " forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n81:\r\n82:Site visit #409 to operations finance captured mailbox exports showing how inventory obsolescence reserve correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precedence.\r\n83:\r\n84:Interview #336 with operations finance highlighted how inventory obsolescence reserve statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n85:\r\n86:Lead reviewer M. Chen noted that inventory obsolescence reserve created reconciliation noise in operations finance during October count. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n87:\r\n88:The committee packet references inventory obsolescence reserve as a contributing factor to "]
[50.455096, "o", "late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n89:\r\n90:## Case Study 01 — Vendor Onboarding Backlog\r\n91:\r\n92:Lead reviewer L. Bergstrom noted that vendor onboarding backlog created reconciliation noise in procurement during Q1 close. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n93:\r\n94:Draft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n95:\r\n96:Follow-up #228 confirmed that procurement had been using an informal spreadsheet for vendor onboarding backlog. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n97:\r\n98:During Q1 close, S. Patel circulated a draft finding on vendor onboarding backlog. Finance operations pushed back"]
[50.455995, "o", ", arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n99:\r\n100:Working paper WP-7827 documents a three-way match failure tied to vendor onboarding backlog. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n101:\r\n102:Memo WP-3161 summarizes stakeholder interviews about vendor onboarding backlog. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n103:\r\n104:Risk assessment WP-7474 ties vendor onboarding backlog to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n105:\r\n106:Interview #571 with procurement highlighted how vendor onboarding backlog statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n107:\r\n"]
[50.456096, "o", "108:Lead reviewer S. Patel noted that vendor onboarding backlog created reconciliation noise in procurement during Q1 close. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n109:\r\n110:Draft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n111:\r\n112:Working paper WP-3773 documents a three-way match failure tied to vendor onboarding backlog. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n113:\r\n114:The committee packet references vendor onboarding backlog as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n115:\r\n116:In Q1 close, external advisors reviewed vendor onboarding backlog and asked for a machine-readabl"]
[50.456349, "o", "e reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n117:\r\n118:Lead reviewer L. Bergstrom noted that vendor onboarding backlog created reconciliation noise in procurement during Q1 close. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n119:\r\n120:Risk assessment WP-2579 ties vendor onboarding backlog to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n121:\r\n122:In Q1 close, external advisors reviewed vendor onboarding backlog and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n123:\r\n124:In Q1 close, external advisors reviewed vendor onboarding backlog and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so a"]
[50.45637, "o", "uditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n125:\r\n126:Draft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n127:\r\n128:Lead reviewer M. Chen noted that vendor onboarding backlog created reconciliation noise in procurement during Q1 close. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n129:\r\n130:In Q1 close, external advisors reviewed vendor onboarding backlog and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n131:\r\n132:The committee packet references vendor onboarding backlog as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n"]
