[205.198402, "o", "     1\t## Investigation Brief 07 — Exception Flags (Part I)\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\tExtract policy (authoritative):\r\n     4\t\r\n     5\tException coding review: `exception_reason` is null unless a code applies. Set\r\n     6\t`over_limit` when `amount_usd` strictly exceeds 10000. Set `compliance_hold`\r\n     7\twhen final status is `rejected`, a qualifying `compliance@` email referenced\r\n     8\tthat transaction, and that email block includes a `sent:` line. The sent-date\r\n     9\tcomparison used for `compliance_hold` is defined in Investigation Brief 09\r\n    10\t(Mid-Year Amendment), not Brief 03. Multiple reasons join with semicolon in\r\n    11\tlexical order of the reason codes.\r\n    12\t\r\n    13\t## Investigation Brief 07 — Exception Flags (Part I) — field notes\r\n    14\t\r\n    15\tMemo WP-7758 summarizes stakeholder interviews about vendor onboarding backlog. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n    16\t\r\n    17\tIn Q1 cl"]
[205.200717, "o", "ose, external advisors reviewed vendor onboarding backlog and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n    18\t\r\n    19\tDuring Q1 close, A. Ndiaye circulated a draft finding on vendor onboarding backlog. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n    20\t\r\n    21\tRisk assessment WP-8021 ties vendor onboarding backlog to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n    22\t\r\n    23\tWorking paper WP-3669 documents a three-way match failure tied to vendor onboarding backlog. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n    24\t\r\n    25\tSite visit #351 to procurement captured mailbox exports showing how vendor onboarding backlog correspo"]
