[205.208216, "o", "     1\t## Investigation Brief 08 — Exception Flags (Part II) and Artifacts\r\n     2\t\r\n     3\tController memo (binding reconciliation rule):\r\n     4\t\r\n     5\tContinued from Brief 07. Set `policy_waiver` when final status is `approved`,\r\n     6\t`amount_usd` > 10000, and a Policy Exception block exists for that transaction\r\n     7\twith `approved_by: compliance` on its own line. Set `retroactive_review` when\r\n     8\tfinal status is `reversed`, `amount_usd` > 5000, and a winning correction\r\n     9\tnotice changed status for that transaction.\r\n    10\t\r\n    11\t`extract --outdir` must write: `transactions.json` as `{\"items\":[...]}` sorted\r\n    12\tby `transaction_id` ascending with fields transaction_id, owner, status\r\n    13\t(lowercase), effective_date, amount_usd, exception_reason (null or\r\n    14\tsemicolon-joined codes). `transactions.csv` uses header\r\n    15\ttransaction_id,owner,status,effective_date,amount_usd,exception_reason with the\r\n    16\tsame rows; leave exception_reason blank when null. `exceptions.json` i"]
