[232.55709, "o", "reserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n    76\t\r\n    77\tRisk assessment WP-5795 ties SOX sampling mismatch to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n    78\t\r\n    79\tInterview #266 with internal audit highlighted how SOX sampling mismatch statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n    80\t\r\n    81\tFollow-up #130 confirmed that internal audit had been using an informal spreadsheet for SOX sampling mismatch. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n    82\t\r\n    83\tFollow-up #559 confirmed that internal audit had been using an informal spreadsheet for SOX sampling mismatch. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structur"]
[232.557107, "o", "ed sections at file end.\r\n    84\t\r\n    85\tMemo WP-7928 summarizes stakeholder interviews about SOX sampling mismatch. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n    86\t\r\n    87\tThe committee packet references SOX sampling mismatch as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n    88\t\r\n    89\tFollow-up #741 confirmed that internal audit had been using an informal spreadsheet for SOX sampling mismatch. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n    90\t\r\n\\n===== TOP /tmp/brief03.md\r\n"]
