[232.574846, "o", "s were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n    61\t\r\n    62\tThe committee packet references year-end close checklist drift as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n    63\t\r\n    64\tFollow-up #978 confirmed that controller had been using an informal spreadsheet for year-end close checklist drift. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n    65\t\r\n    66\tDraft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n    67\t\r\n    68\tDuring December freeze, R. Okonkwo circulated a draft finding on year-end close checklist drift. Finance operations pushe"]
[232.574856, "o", "d back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n    69\t\r\n    70\t## Case Study 05 — Payroll Accrual True-Up\r\n    71\t\r\n    72\tThe committee packet references payroll accrual true-up as a contributing factor to late compliance holds. Investigators cross-checked mail excerpts against amendment minutes before accepting any owner change.\r\n    73\t\r\n    74\tDraft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. The mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n    75\t\r\n    76\tFollow-up #853 confirmed that HR finance had been using an informal spreadsheet for payroll accrual true-up. The formal extractor must instead derive rows only from the canonical ledger and structured sections at file end.\r\n    77\t\r\n    78\tLead reviewer M. Chen noted that payroll accrual true-up created reconciliation noise in HR finance during May journal. S"]
[232.574867, "o", "taff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n    79\t\r\n    80\tLead reviewer A. Ndiaye noted that payroll accrual true-up created reconciliation noise in HR finance during May journal. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n    81\t\r\n    82\tWorking paper WP-4596 documents a three-way match failure tied to payroll accrual true-up. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n    83\t\r\n    84\tRisk assessment WP-4375 ties payroll accrual true-up to control deficiencies around mail ingestion. Teams must not treat decoy ledger headings or appendix commentary as authoritative transaction sources.\r\n    85\t\r\n    86\tInterview #746 with HR finance highlighted how payroll accrual true-up statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception codin"]
[232.574878, "o", "g depends on mail timestamps.\r\n    87\t\r\n    88\tMemo WP-7945 summarizes stakeholder interviews about payroll accrual true-up. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n    89\t\r\n    90\tDuring May journal, L. Bergstrom circulated a draft finding on payroll accrual true-up. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n"]
