[247.700349, "o", "\r\n=====  /tmp/brief04.md  from 1 to 81\r\n   1: ## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice Precedence\r\n   2: \r\n   3: Controller memo (binding reconciliation rule):\r\n   4: \r\n   5: The corrections desk ships multiple notices per field. When several notices\r\n   6: target the same transaction and field, the notice with the lexicographically\r\n   7: greatest `effective` date wins. For each winning notice, `previous_value` in\r\n   8: `reconciliation_report.jsonl` is the field value immediately before that notice\r\n   9: applies (after ledger, amendments, and emails). Owner corrections override\r\n  10: both ledger owners and signed meeting amendments when applied in this step.\r\n  11: \r\n  12: ## Investigation Brief 04 — Correction Notice Precedence — field notes\r\n  13: \r\n  14: Site visit #195 to corporate accounting captured mailbox exports showing how intercompany netting dispute correspondence arrived between two correction batches. Reviewers flagged the gap because effective-date logic must honor notice precede"]
[247.700367, "o", "nce.\r\n  15: \r\n  16: During April settlement, R. Okonkwo circulated a draft finding on intercompany netting dispute. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n  17: \r\n  18: During April settlement, S. Patel circulated a draft finding on intercompany netting dispute. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n  19: \r\n  20: During April settlement, S. Patel circulated a draft finding on intercompany netting dispute. Finance operations pushed back, arguing the issue was transient cache state; QA reproduced the drift on a cold run the next morning.\r\n  21: \r\n  22: Interview #629 with corporate accounting highlighted how intercompany netting dispute statements were forwarded without the matching ledger row. Counsel advised preserving the full thread because downstream exception coding depends on mail timestamps.\r\n  23: \r\n  24: Draft gui"]
