[443.290233, "o", "\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[443.296848, "o", "## Investigation Brief 03 — Compliance Mail Timing\r\n\r\nExtract policy (authoritative):\r\n\r\nThe March mail-room audit explained missing holds: agents applied compliance\r\nmessages without checking dispatch dates. When an excerpt includes\r\n`sent: YYYY-MM-DD`, apply the status change only if sent is greater than or\r\nequal to the ledger date for that transaction. When no `sent:` line is present,\r\napply the status change if precedence allows. Correction notices always apply\r\nafter ledger rows, meeting amendments, and mail excerpts have been merged.\r\n\r\n## Investigation Brief 03 — Compliance Mail Timing — field notes\r\n\r\nLead reviewer M. Chen noted that year-end close checklist drift created reconciliation noise in controller during December freeze. Staff initially blamed tooling, but timeline reconstruction showed manual overrides arriving after batch lock.\r\n\r\nDraft guidance in this paragraph is non-binding: some early tooling compared compliance mail against post-correction effective dates when flagging holds. T"]
[443.299287, "o", "he mid-year amendment later in this archive supersedes that draft practice.\r\n\r\nMemo WP-3037 summarizes stakeholder interviews about year-end close checklist drift. Participants disagreed on whether unsigned amendments should ever override ledger owners; Brief 05 resolves that question for the extractor.\r\n\r\nIn December freeze, external advisors reviewed year-end close checklist drift and asked for a machine-readable reconciliation trace. The archive preserves narrative context so auditors can explain why a given transaction received compliance_hold.\r\n\r\nWorking paper WP-7415 documents a three-way match failure tied to year-end close checklist drift. The team escalated when repeated extractor runs produced different status columns for the same transaction id.\r\n\r\n"]
[443.302889, "o", "\u001b[?2004hroot@7a65087374e8:/app# "]
[505.574514, "i", "apply_patch <<'PATCH'\n*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: audit-extractor/src/parser/ledger.js\n@@\n function parseLedger(markdown) {\n-  const start = markdown.indexOf(\"## Transaction Ledger\");\n-  if (start < 0) {\n-    return [];\n-  }\n-  const slice = markdown.slice(start);\n-  const rows = [];\n-  const blocks = slice.split(/^### /m).slice(1);\n-  for (const block of blocks) {\n-    const lines = block.split(\"\\n\");\n-    const transactionId = lines[0].trim();\n-    if (!transactionId.startsWith(\"TXN-\")) {\n-      continue;\n-    }\n-    if (rows.some((row) => row.transaction_id === transactionId)) {\n-      continue;\n-    }\n-    const row = { transaction_id: transactionId };\n-    for (const line of lines) {\n-      const trimmed = line.trim();\n-      if (trimmed.startsWith(\"amount:\")) {\n-        row.amount = Number(trimmed.split(\":\")[1].trim());\n-      } else if (trimmed.startsWith(\"owner:\")) {\n-        row.owner = trimmed.split(\":\")[1].trim();\n-      } else if (trimmed.startsWith(\"status:\")) {\n-        row.status = trimmed"]
[505.574643, "i", ".split(\":\")[1].trim();\n-      } else if (trimmed.startsWith(\"date:\")) {\n-        row.date = trimmed.split(\":\")[1].trim();\n-      }\n-    }\n-    rows.push(row);\n-  }\n-  return rows;\n+  // Binding rule (Brief 01): only the section whose heading line is exactly\n+  // '## Transaction Ledger' is authoritative. Ignore working-copy headings.\n+  const startMatch = markdown.match(/^## Transaction Ledger\\s*$/m);\n+  if (!startMatch || startMatch.index == null) return [];\n+\n+  const start = startMatch.index;\n+  const afterStart = markdown.slice(start);\n+  // Stop at next top-level heading (\"## \") after the ledger heading.\n+  const nextTop = afterStart.slice(startMatch[0].length).match(/^##\\s+/m);\n+  const slice = nextTop\n+    ? afterStart.slice(0, nextTop.index + startMatch[0].length)\n+    : afterStart;\n+\n+  const rows = [];\n+  const blocks = slice.split(/^### /m).slice(1);\n+  for (const block of blocks) {\n+    // Ignore provisional ledger blocks entirely.\n+    if (/^provisional:\\s*true\\s*$/im.test(block)) continue;\n+    "]
[505.574657, "i", "const lines = block.split(\"\\n\");\n+    const transactionId = lines[0].trim();\n+    if (!transactionId.startsWith(\"TXN-\")) continue;\n+    const row = { transaction_id: transactionId };\n+    for (const line of lines) {\n+      const trimmed = line.trim();\n+      if (trimmed.startsWith(\"amount:\")) {\n+        row.amount = Number(trimmed.split(\":\")[1].trim());\n+      } else if (trimmed.startsWith(\"owner:\")) {\n+        row.owner = trimmed.split(\":\")[1].trim();\n+      } else if (trimmed.startsWith(\"status:\")) {\n+        row.status = trimmed.split(\":\")[1].trim();\n+      } else if (trimmed.startsWith(\"date:\")) {\n+        row.date = trimmed.split(\":\")[1].trim();\n+      }\n+    }\n+    rows.push(row);\n+  }\n+  return rows;\n }\n*** End Patch\nPATCH\n"]
[505.574993, "o", "apply_patch <<'PATCH'"]
